Subject: [PATCH] mtk: sugov: bypass direction delays for forced updates

sugov_should_update_freq() intentionally bypasses its rate limit for a
changed policy limit or increased deadline bandwidth. However, the next
stage applies the up/down delay unconditionally and can reject that
forced update. Honor need_freq_update at both stages.

Ordinary transitions still use the configured direction delays. Keep
the forced flag until an update is accepted; retain the vendor workload
and enqueue checks, driver calls, policy limits and thermal protection.
Zero-delay policies retain the same decision results.

This targets the Rodin vendor scheduler module, not the common boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/cpufreq_sugov_main.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/cpufreq_sugov_main.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/cpufreq_sugov_main.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/sugov/cpufreq_sugov_main.c
@@ -195,7 +195,8 @@
 static bool sugov_update_next_freq(struct sugov_policy *sg_policy, u64 time,
 				   unsigned int next_freq)
 {
-	if (sugov_up_down_rate_limit(sg_policy, time, next_freq))
+	if (!sg_policy->need_freq_update &&
+	    sugov_up_down_rate_limit(sg_policy, time, next_freq))
 		return false;
 
 	if (sg_policy->need_freq_update || wl_dsu_cnt_cached != wl_dsu_delay_ch_cnt ||
